{"name":"Hole in One","hex":"#4aae97","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hole in one","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hole that is completed by sinking the ball in a single shot or attempt, with one hit.","Any rare, wonderful, or remarkable accomplishment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hole_in_one"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hole in one","blocks":[{"text":"In golf, a hole in one or hole-in-one occurs when a ball hit from the tee on the first stroke of a hole finishes in the cup. Holes-in-one most commonly occur on par 3 holes, the shortest holes on a standard size golf course. Longer hitters have also recorded holes-in-one on longer holes, though nearly all par-4 and par-5 holes are too long for golfers to reach in a single shot. Although holes-in one generally require an accurate, well-hit shot, they also involve a significant amount of luck. As of January 2021, a condor hole-in-one on a par-5 hole had been recorded on five occasions."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hole_in_one","wikidata":"Q1337788"},{"title":"Hole in One (2010 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Hole in One is a 2010 American sports sex comedy film starring Steve Talley, David Ellison, K. T. Tatara, Dean Cameron, Christopher Showerman and Dean Cain."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Hole_in_One_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hole_in_One_(2010_film)","wikidata":"Q3139312"},{"title":"Hole","blocks":[{"text":"A hole is an opening in or through a particular medium, usually a solid body. Holes occur through natural and artificial processes, and may be useful for various purposes, or may represent a problem needing to be addressed in many fields of engineering. Depending on the material and the placement, a hole may be an indentation in a surface, or may pass completely through that surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Hole_in_wood.jpg/330px-Hole_in_wood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hole","wikidata":"Q20204151"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Hole_in_One_Golfer.jpg/500px-Hole_in_One_Golfer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Hole_in_One_Golfer.jpg/500px-Hole_in_One_Golfer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An amateur golfer celebrates a hole in one.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHole_in_One_Golfer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Hole_in_One_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Hole_in_One_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHole_in_One_Poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Hole_in_wood.jpg/500px-Hole_in_wood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Hole_in_wood.jpg/1280px-Hole_in_wood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Hole_in_wood.jpg/500px-Hole_in_wood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A hole through a dead tree","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHole_in_wood.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Stamp_US_1954_2c_Jefferson_coil_pair.jpg/500px-Stamp_US_1954_2c_Jefferson_coil_pair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Stamp_US_1954_2c_Jefferson_coil_pair.jpg/500px-Stamp_US_1954_2c_Jefferson_coil_pair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Perforation holes between a pair of postage stamps from a coil of stamps","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStamp_US_1954_2c_Jefferson_coil_pair.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/Mug_and_Torus_morph.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/Mug_and_Torus_morph.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"In geometric topology, the doughnut and the coffee cup are considered to fall into the same mathematical \"genus\" because each has one hole.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMug_and_Torus_morph.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Drill_-_Hole_Types.png/500px-Drill_-_Hole_Types.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Drill_-_Hole_Types.png/500px-Drill_-_Hole_Types.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hole types in engineering: blind (left), through (middle), interrupted (right).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADrill_-_Hole_Types.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Pothole_in_Villeray%2C_Montr%C3%A9al.jpg/500px-Pothole_in_Villeray%2C_Montr%C3%A9al.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Pothole_in_Villeray%2C_Montr%C3%A9al.jpg/1280px-Pothole_in_Villeray%2C_Montr%C3%A9al.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Pothole_in_Villeray%2C_Mo